<title>INDIA: India silver drops on spurt in arrivals, gold dips.</title>
<headline>India silver drops on spurt in arrivals, gold dips.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Silver prices opened on a weak note and extended losses towards the close on the back of increased arrivals, dealer said.</p>
<p>&quot;Reports of setback in the world market as well as absence of fresh demand from the industrial consumers aided the weak sentiment,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>Gold opened on a steady note but moved down towards the close on fresh supplies. Gold biscuit (116.50 gramme) settled 100 rupees lower at 60,400 rupees per piece.  </p>
